# {{project_name}}

FastAPI microservice generated by `backend-service-generator`.

The generator writes a ready-to-use `.env` (a copy of `.env.example`) and
`docker-compose.yml` loads it via `env_file`, so `docker compose up` picks up
your configuration. `.env` is gitignored; commit changes to `.env.example`
to share new defaults.

## Quick start

```bash
# Install dependencies (creates .venv)
uv sync

# Run database migrations
uv run alembic upgrade head

# Start server (console script from [project.scripts])
uv run {{project_name}}
```

The console script points at `{{project_name}}.__main__:main`, so
`uv run python -m {{project_name}}` works identically.

## Make targets

A `Makefile` wraps the common workflows. Run `make help` to list them all:

```bash
make install      # uv sync
make dev          # run locally with auto-reload
make test         # uv run pytest
make lint         # uv run ruff check .
make migrate      # uv run alembic upgrade head
make docker-up    # docker compose up -d (api + db)
make docker-down  # docker compose down
make docker-logs  # follow api logs
```

## CI

The repository is initialized with CI for your hosting provider —
`.github/workflows/ci.yml` on GitHub or `.gitlab-ci.yml` on GitLab. The
pipeline runs `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy`, `pytest` and a
docker build.
